I searched the AI Index several ways and couldn't find which of these checkboxes are unchecked by default.

The index does confirm what the "Personalize List Columns" dialog contains. It has six settings checkboxes: **Wrap column text**, **Compact rows**, **Active row highlighting**, **Modern cell coloring**, **Enable list edit** and **Double click to edit**. None of the stored entries say whether each one starts checked or unchecked, for the Users list or any other list. I'd rather not guess which two are off.

\boxed{\text{Unknown — the AI Index does not record which checkboxes are unchecked by default}}

I couldn't find this in the knowledge base, so I can't say whether it's true or false.

The only thing it records about the avatar on the Users list page (sys_user_list.do) is that "Avatar" is one of the fields you can pick in the field search. Nothing describes what the avatar shows when no image has been uploaded, and nothing mentions initials. I searched several ways (avatar, initials, photo, no image, profile picture) and found nothing more.

\boxed{Unknown}

**True.** "Peripherals" is a valid Service Catalog category.

The AI Index lists it as one of the catalog's top-level categories: Services, Can We Help You?, Office, Peripherals, Hardware, Software, Desktops and Mobiles. At least one item is filed under it: the Belkin iPad Mini Case, listed under Peripherals at $50.00. The Catalog Items list (`sc_cat_item_list.do`) has a Category column you can filter on. No record lists the exact values in that column's filter dropdown, so this answer is based on the category list above.

\boxed{True}

I don't know. The AI Index doesn't say which header buttons appear on a knowledge article page after you open it from the Knowledge search results, so I can't name the new button.

The index does describe the Knowledge search-results list page (`kb_knowledge_list.do`): its header controls are "Show / hide filter", "Show / hide natural language filter", a field search dropdown, an "Actions on selected rows" dropdown and a "New" button. It also has facts about specific articles (KB0010142, KB0010143, KB0010017), but none of them describe the article page's layout. I searched several ways, including article page, article form, header actions and specific article numbers, and none of the results covered it.

\boxed{\text{Unknown — not recorded in the AI Index}}

I couldn't find this in the AI Index. I searched it several ways, including for "IP-Router-3", "Configuration item", reference-field icons, and preview and dependency-map icons. None of the results say how many icons show up next to the Configuration item field after a value is entered.

The closest match is a note on the Change Request form's Configuration item field. It says typing a name straight into the field can fail with "Match not found, reset to original" and an "Invalid update" error. The fix it gives is to click the "Look up value for field: Configuration item" button and pick the item from the list. It doesn't say what icons appear after that.

\boxed{I don't know}

I couldn't find the answer in the AI Index after several searches, so I don't know how many preapproved model cards show a 100% success rate.

The closest thing it has is a description of the Create Change Request landing page (`sn_chg_model_ui_landing.do`). It has four tabs: Pinned, Models, Preapproved and All, and the Models tab includes the Emergency and Normal models. None of the stored notes list the preapproved model cards or their success rates.

